<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar inflows $116.2 mln on May 9.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar inflows $116.2 mln on May 9.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $116.2 million surplus on May 9 in the commercial foreign exchange market, according to Central Bank data supplied to banks.</p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the Central Bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON MAY 9</p>
<p>Exports: $278.5 million</p>
<p>Imports: $230.7 million</p>
<p>Finanancial buy: $292 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $223.6 million</p>
<p>Net surplus: $116.2 million</p>
<p>MAY DOLLAR FLOWS UP DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $1.472 billion</p>
<p>Imports: $1.449 billion</p>
<p>Financial buy: $2.638 billion</p>
<p>Financial sell: $1.533 billion</p>
<p>Net surplus: $1.128 billion</p>
<p>NOTE: The figures were rounded off.</p>
<p>((--Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo Newsroon 55 11 2485418))</p>
